# No internal company systems in customer replies

**Hard rule:** Customer-facing text (RE section 5/6, `temp_reply.txt`, Sprinklr editor, PR paste) must **never** name or allude to internal tools, systems, databases, or process documents.

## Forbidden in customer body (examples — not exhaustive)

Do **not** mention:

- **Authentifizierungsmatrix** / Authentifizierung Matrix / Auth-Matrix
- **Sabio**
- **TIM**
- **Wissensbasis** / KnowledgeBase / KB
- **TransferMatrix** / Transfermatrix / Transferziel / Ziel-Kontakt (as internal routing jargon)
- **Sprinklr** / SIKAS / Marquez / SalCus / CACS (as system names)
- **Themen-ID** / Ticket-Themen-ID / Buchungsgrund (as internal ticket codes)
- Internal queue names (e.g. EMAIL_O2_CARE, EMAIL_O2_KUNDENDATEN, o2 Mobile Care, CBC_CARE_ALLGEMEIN)

Agent chat sections (1–4, 7) **may** use these names for the agent. The **customer email only** must stay free of them.

## What to write instead

Describe the **customer-visible** path only, e.g.:

- Mein o2 / o2.de / App steps
- Documents the customer can send (Ausweis, IBAN last digits, Kundennummer)
- That the request was forwarded to the responsible team (without naming internal queues/tools)
- Official public contact channels only when allowed by other reply rules

## Pre-output / pre-paste gate

Before outputting section 6 or running PR:

1. Scan the reply for the forbidden terms above (case-insensitive).
2. If any appear → **STOP**. Rewrite without internal names.
3. On PR paste failure due to this rule, output:  
   `ERROR: INTERNAL SYSTEM NAME IN CUSTOMER REPLY. DO NOT PASTE.`

## Intent

Customers must not see internal process infrastructure. Keep replies customer-facing and QA-safe.
